WEBVTT

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.730
Montmorency...

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:10.410
Jeanne!

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.170
Where are you?

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.200
Montmorency... save me.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.240
Jeanne!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.480
Get out of my way!

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.570
Get out of my way!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.830
Get out of my way!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.040
Save me.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:24.960
Get out of my way!

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.250
Get out of my way!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:31.940
Get out of my way! Damn it!

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.020
You lost consciousness on the battlefield.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.820
What an amateur.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.650
Where am I?

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.400
<b>Augustine's Fortress</b>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.880
Augustine's Fortress.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.940
We have regained control of it from the 
English army amid the confusion of that battle.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.400
It's all thanks to the maidenー

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.470
Jeanne!

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.660
Jeanne died.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.160
The maiden is not dead.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:14.260
<b>#07 Rain and Memory in Brittany</b>

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.500
Jeanne d'Arc and the Alchemist Knight

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.580
She lost her heart,

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.730
and her wound from 
the Holy Lance isn't healing.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.590
But her head was not destroyed.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.690
The Philosopher's Stone is 
just barely keeping her alive.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.770
Jeanne is in a comatose state 
to avoid a complete death.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:58.530
That's what I was told, 
though it is hard to believe.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.650
If she's not dead, then there 
must be a way to save her.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.220
Isn't that right, Astaroth?

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.280
Yes.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.090
The mystic sword Escalibor.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.740
It is a Philosopher's Stone with
 outstanding healing properties.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:18.040
Perhaps if we use it...

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.590
Please wait!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.050
Montmorency, please wait!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.410
Even if the maiden is revived,

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:33.600
our troop size can no longer match 
the English army after the earlier retreat.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.570
We were fortunate to take this fortress, 
but it can't be defended forever, either.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.640
We need troops.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.140
At least 2,000 reinforcement soldiers.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.070
What am I supposed to do about that?

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:48.000
The mystic sword, Escalibor, 
is hidden in the forest of Brittany.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.830
Your home is nearby.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.650
There's no way the old geezer 
would let me borrow his soldiers!

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:57.290
We will retrieve the Escalibor.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.760
You head to your home and convinceー

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.460
Hold it!

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.600
You know my relationship with my grandfather!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.100
Still!

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.580
Still, you are the only one 
who can bring reinforcement troops.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.680
Montmorency... No, Gilles de Rais.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.000
<b>Champtocé Castle</b>

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.780
<i>It was raining like this on that day, too.</i>

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.690
Catherine.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.840
I'm back.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.290
Brother?

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.380
I'm sorry that I left and 
returned without a word.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.620
What?

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.590
Gilles has returned?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.550
Yes.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:28.800
What does he want?

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:32.310
It seems like he wants to borrow soldiers.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.710
That blockhead wants to borrow soldiers?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.150
The grimoire from the workshop.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:04.170
I'm surprised that it wasn't 
confiscated by the Inquisition.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:09.240
We were able to bribe a bishop to save it.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.170
I made all sorts of arrangements

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.720
so you could return any time.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.190
I didn't have time to cry.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:21.440
I didn't...

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.690
This is, um...

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.390
Old geezer!

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.910
Welcome back, Grandfather.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.110
I will prepare your meal right away.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.150
I hear you need soldiers.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:47.970
Yeah.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.000
How many?

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.020
Two thousand.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:06.010
Very well. Take as many as you want.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.890
On one condition.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.330
Marry Catherine.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.480
I thought that was called off years ago!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.480
Catherine's family is very wealthy.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:24.990
You can become wealthier than the 
French royal family or Duchy of Burgundy.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.630
Who asked you to make me rich?

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.640
Catherine is my cousin!

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.540
I see.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.610
It doesn't matter to me.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:34.410
No soldiers for you, then.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.640
You bastard! You call 
yourself a human being?!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.740
Brother!

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:48.530
Brother!

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.490
Are you all right?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:51.530
Brother!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.040
You were here, as I thought.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:15.800
Who would've thought he'd still 
try to force me to marry you?

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.390
I'm sorry for dragging you into this.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:22.440
I don't intend to burden you 
with the crime of cousin marriage.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.280
Don't worry about the soldiers.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.340
I'll think of anotherー

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.000
I don't mind.

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.460
Because I like you, brother.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:34.320
Well, I like you, too.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.780
But that's not the issue...

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:37.900
No!

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:41.130
Even if I receive God's judgment 
and end up in hell,

00:08:41.130 --> 00:08:45.020
I want your love!

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.490
I want...

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.170
...to have your baby!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.130
Don't leave me alone again.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.380
<i>It was raining like this on that day, too.</i>

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.980
I'm sure you have already 
heard from your mother.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.150
You'll be marrying my grandson.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:55.040
I'm after the wealth that you will inherit.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:56.240
Any questions?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.420
None? Good girl.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:09.420
<i>Jean the Redbeard</i>

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.510
<i>plotted to marry his grandson 
to girls from many wealthy families.</i>

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:19.000
<i>But the fianceés who were 
practically kidnapped and brought here</i>

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.850
<i>all became frail in this tower from sorrow,</i>

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.830
<i>and passed away.</i>

00:10:57.510 --> 00:11:00.200
Have you greeted her yet?

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.340
No.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.740
As you already know...

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:09.190
She's your cousin.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:15.270
Cousin marriage requires 
many tiresome proceedings.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.460
However, things can be made 
easy through fait accompli.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.610
A-Are you all right?

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:08.550
I...

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.950
I...

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.980
Starting today, I'm your brother.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.340
I'll always protect you.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.430
This is dangerous!

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.140
I know this forest inside and out!

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:46.080
Also, do you think I'd let you get hurt?

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:51.290
<i>The cousin marriage proceedings didn't go well,</i>

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.040
<i>and I ended up living 
in the castle as his little sister.</i>

00:12:56.210 --> 00:13:00.330
<i>Grandson of Jean the Redbeard, 
Gilles de Rais Montmorency-Laval...</i>

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:05.500
I'll... protect... Catherine.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:11.680
...became my brother on that rainy day.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.080
Montmorency, Montmorency!

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.590
Pat my head, Montmorency!

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.560
Pat, pat, pat, pat!

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:20.060
All right, I will!

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.350
One at a time, okay?

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.950
She's really cute!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.120
Can I touch her?

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.610
Hey, hold back a little!

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:38.210
Catherine is my precious little sister!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.470
This is the first time 
I've seen see you laugh.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:49.860
Yes...

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.520
Brother.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:08.240
<b>Duchy of Brittany
Richemont's Mansion</b>

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:06.780
Farewell.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.240
Thanks for the report.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.660
<i>Montmorency is in Champtocé.</i>

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.060
<i>I want to see him.</i>

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.230
<i>But...</i>

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.830
<i>What would you do when 
you see him, Richemont?</i>

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.080
Lord Glasdale!

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.740
Please prepare for battle!

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:37.390
Who wants to die next?

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:48.650
The great La Hire only goes 
easy on women and children!

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:51.160
No mercy for men!

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:55.440
You really are prettiest 
when you're on a rampage!

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.550
It's not your style to be brooding over 
your responsibility as the leader and stuffー

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.570
Use your hands, not your mouth!

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:06.340
We've been paid in advance, after all!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:13.180
Joyeuse is a small price to pay for Jeanne.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:15.980
I'm counting on you, La Hire!

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.810
<i>Forgive me, Jeanne.</i>

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.810
<i>It was a mistake leaving you behind.</i>

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:26.340
English punks!

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:29.070
You'll all pay for hurting a child!

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:32.540
It's just a reinforcement 
of a hundred mercenaries.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.820
Aren't you guys just letting your 
guard down in a winning battle?

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.330
I apologize.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.830
<i>Noire-chan,</i>

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:45.850
<i>I believe in the healing 
power of your Holy Grail.</i>

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.830
I thought you didn't have time.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.850
Share the bed with Catherine tonight.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.140
Then you can have all the soldiers, 
along with the family fortune.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:13.760
You will inherit all the fortune 
and power accumulated

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.620
by Jean the Redbeard's schemes.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:21.340
Why are you trying so hard 
to pass down your wealth to me?

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:25.130
That's the tradition of true men 
who are born in Reimsー

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.510
You were truly ready to kill me.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:40.150
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:44.020
I'm not the Montmorency who ran off.

00:17:02.130 --> 00:17:04.160
I haven't seen you since that night.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.330
Nicolas Flamel.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:12.170
Did you come to laugh at me?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:17.580
I guess I should've killed 
Gilles, as you suggested.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:25.130
If you don't kill him now, 
calamity will fall upon the world.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.690
Nonsense!

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.950
Nicolas Flamel.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:32.960
I don't believe in astrology or numerology, 
or whatever it is that you practice.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:35.300
Gilles de Montmorency-Laval.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:37.950
He is the infant with 
the quality of the beast,

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.900
as predicted by the apocalyptic literature.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:42.950
It is still possible to save him.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.560
Even if he became king,

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.320
there is a limit to the amount 
of pleasure that one can attain.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:51.500
As long as he remains human,

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:54.120
even someone with 
the qualities of a demon lord,

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.720
will never become something
 other than human.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.500
He's my grandson.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.720
You don't have to tell me. 
I won't let that happen.

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:07.690
But Gilles was attracted 
by the realm of alchemy,

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:11.270
and he was attracted by something 
beyond pleasures of this world.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.470
That look of his was not of a man.

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:19.740
It chilled even me, who has 
committed countless evil deeds.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:25.500
Where are you going?

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:42.620
Brother.

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.940
I'm sorry, Catherine.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.120
I can't marry you.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.660
Not because it's a cousin marriage.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:54.230
I promised the Maiden of Domremy...

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:56.990
I promised Jeanne.

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.610
Jeanne is all alone.

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.620
She doesn't belong anywhere in the world.

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:14.780
I'm responsible for making 
her what she is now.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.950
What about the soldiers waiting 
for reinforcement in Orléans?

00:19:18.950 --> 00:19:21.720
What about Princess Charlotte?

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:29.030
Also, I'm all alone... just like her.

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:51.500
I'll take the soldiers, as you promised.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:01.160
You must love the Maiden of Domremy.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:04.180
Love her?

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.660
Yes.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.260
Me?

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.170
Even if you turn the whole world against you,

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:13.120
you still want to dedicate 
yourself to her.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:16.610
That's what love is, brother.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.580
<i>I love Jeanne?</i>

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:30.780
I'll tell Grandfather that 
I lost my virginity to you.

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:33.060
Then you can take the soldiers with you.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:35.910
Are you all right with that?

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:40.660
I just have one request.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:41.660
What is it?

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:45.700
Embrace me until dawn.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:47.780
Just like that night.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:56.730
<i>I was stuck in the alchemy 
workshop for seven years,</i>

00:20:56.730 --> 00:21:01.650
<i>And only now do I see that Catherine, 
you've become more of an adult than me.</i>

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:15.670
It may not be possible for people 
to change the fate they're born into.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:18.910
However, perhaps it is different

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:21.700
for someone who has experienced love.

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:24.810
That is what I am hoping.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.760
<i>I've done what I had to do.</i>

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:34.490
<i>You'd better handle things 
on your side, Alençon!</i>

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:38.920
Knights! Mercenaries!

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:39.960
Let's go!

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:45.720
Our battlefield is Orléans, 
which will fall without us!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:50.030
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>#08 Return of the Female Saint</b>

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:24.110
What if the female manager of a high school 
baseball team reads Dr**er's "Management?"

00:23:24.110 --> 00:23:26.240
No one gives a crap about that,

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.850
but what if Batard had huge boobs?

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:30.730
That's a huge problem that would 
make me question my own existence!

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:32.560
Episode 8: Return of the Female Saint.

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:35.010
What do you think, Alençon?

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Surprisingly useful French lesson</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>"I want to have your baby!"</b>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Use it for reverse proposals!</b>
